  57:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c **** 
  58:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c **** /** @defgroup PWREx_Exported_Functions_Group1 Peripheral Extended features functions 
  59:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****   *  @brief Peripheral Extended features functions 
  60:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****   *
  61:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c **** @verbatim   
  62:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c **** 
  63:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****  ===============================================================================
  64:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****                  ##### Peripheral extended features functions #####
  65:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****  ===============================================================================
  66:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c **** 
  67:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****     *** Main and Backup Regulators configuration ***
  68:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****     ================================================
  69:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****     [..] 
  70:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****       (+) The backup domain includes 4 Kbytes of backup SRAM accessible only from 
  71:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           the CPU, and address in 32-bit, 16-bit or 8-bit mode. Its content is 
  72:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           retained even in Standby or VBAT mode when the low power backup regulator
  73:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           is enabled. It can be considered as an internal EEPROM when VBAT is 
  74:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           always present. You can use the HAL_PWREx_EnableBkUpReg() function to 
  75:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           enable the low power backup regulator. 
  76:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c **** 
  77:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****       (+) When the backup domain is supplied by VDD (analog switch connected to VDD) 
  78:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           the backup SRAM is powered from VDD which replaces the VBAT power supply to 
  79:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           save battery life.
  80:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c **** 
  81:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****       (+) The backup SRAM is not mass erased by a tamper event. It is read 
  82:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           protected to prevent confidential data, such as cryptographic private 
  83:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           key, from being accessed. The backup SRAM can be erased only through 
  84:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           the Flash interface when a protection level change from level 1 to 
  85:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           level 0 is requested. 
  86:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****       -@- Refer to the description of Read protection (RDP) in the Flash 
  87:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           programming manual.
  88:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c **** 
  89:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****       (+) The main internal regulator can be configured to have a tradeoff between 
  90:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           performance and power consumption when the device does not operate at 
  91:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           the maximum frequency. This is done through __HAL_PWR_MAINREGULATORMODE_CONFIG() 
  92:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           macro which configure VOS bit in PWR_CR register
  93:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           
  94:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****         Refer to the product datasheets for more details.
  95:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c **** 
  96:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****     *** FLASH Power Down configuration ****
  97:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****     =======================================
  98:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****     [..] 
  99:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****       (+) By setting the FPDS bit in the PWR_CR register by using the 
 100:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           HAL_PWREx_EnableFlashPowerDown() function, the Flash memory also enters power 
 101:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           down mode when the device enters Stop mode. When the Flash memory 
 102:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           is in power down mode, an additional startup delay is incurred when 
 103:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           waking up from Stop mode.
 104:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           
 105:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****            (+) For STM32F42xxx/43xxx/446xx/469xx/479xx Devices, the scale can be modified only when
 106:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****            is OFF and the HSI or HSE clock source is selected as system clock. 
 107:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****            The new value programmed is active only when the PLL is ON.
 108:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****            When the PLL is OFF, the voltage scale 3 is automatically selected. 
 109:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****         Refer to the datasheets for more details.
 110:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c **** 
 111:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****     *** Over-Drive and Under-Drive configuration ****
 112:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****     =================================================
 113:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****     [..]         
 114:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****        (+) For STM32F42xxx/43xxx/446xx/469xx/479xx Devices, in Run mode: the main regulator has
 115:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****            2 operating modes available:
 116:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****         (++) Normal mode: The CPU and core logic operate at maximum frequency at a given 
 117:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****              voltage scaling (scale 1, scale 2 or scale 3)
 118:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****         (++) Over-drive mode: This mode allows the CPU and the core logic to operate at a 
 119:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****             higher frequency than the normal mode for a given voltage scaling (scale 1,  
 120:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****             scale 2 or scale 3). This mode is enabled through HAL_PWREx_EnableOverDrive() function 
 121:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****             disabled by HAL_PWREx_DisableOverDrive() function, to enter or exit from Over-drive mod
 122:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****             the sequence described in Reference manual.
 123:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****              
 124:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****        (+) For STM32F42xxx/43xxx/446xx/469xx/479xx Devices, in Stop mode: the main regulator or low
 125:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****            supplies a low power voltage to the 1.2V domain, thus preserving the content of register
 126:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****            and internal SRAM. 2 operating modes are available:
 127:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****          (++) Normal mode: the 1.2V domain is preserved in nominal leakage mode. This mode is only 
 128:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****               available when the main regulator or the low power regulator is used in Scale 3 or 
 129:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****               low voltage mode.
 130:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****          (++) Under-drive mode: the 1.2V domain is preserved in reduced leakage mode. This mode is 
 131:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****               available when the main regulator or the low power regulator is in low voltage mode.
